WEBVTT

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.080
I put my ear down to the ground, tried to hear what the old roots say.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.780
I put my ear down to the ground, tried to hear what the old roots say.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.820
Ain't no silence down there, brother — there's a world going on today.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.500
Signals running through the dark, tree to tree without a sound.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:50.220
Signals running through the dark, tree to tree without a sound.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.500
A million years of talking low, deep beneath this ground.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.680
When the dry wind hits the forest, somebody sends the warning out.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.440
When the dry wind hits the forest, somebody sends the warning out.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.220
Carbon flows and water follows — that's what life is all about.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.320
We put our sensors in the soil, we started listening too.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.350
We put our sensors in the soil, we started listening too.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.660
And what we heard down in the dark — it changed our point of view.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.920
We're listening together now, you and me and all the trees.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:01.270
We're listening together now, you and me and all the trees.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:17.030
Maybe that's the oldest wisdom — learning how to just be.

